# Sample API Requests for Testing Order Saga

## Create a Successful Order

POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-001",
  "shippingAddress": "123 Main St, New York, NY 10001",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "PROD-001",
      "productName": "Laptop",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": 1200.00
    },
    {
      "productId": "PROD-002",
      "productName": "Mouse",
      "quantity": 2,
      "price": 25.00
    }
  ]
}

###

## Create Another Order (Different Customer)

POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-002",
  "shippingAddress": "456 Oak Ave, Los Angeles, CA 90001",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "PROD-003",
      "productName": "Keyboard",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": 75.00
    },
    {
      "productId": "PROD-004",
      "productName": "Monitor",
      "quantity": 2,
      "price": 350.00
    }
  ]
}

###

## Create Order with Multiple Items

POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-003",
  "shippingAddress": "789 Pine Rd, Chicago, IL 60601",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "PROD-005",
      "productName": "Smartphone",
      "quantity": 2,
      "price": 899.99
    },
    {
      "productId": "PROD-006",
      "productName": "Tablet",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": 599.99
    },
    {
      "productId": "PROD-007",
      "productName": "Smartwatch",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": 299.99
    }
  ]
}

###

## Check Order Status (Replace {orderId} with actual order ID from response)

GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders/{orderId}/status

###

## Notes:
# 1. Copy the orderId from the POST response
# 2. Replace {orderId} in the GET request with the actual ID
# 3. The saga orchestrator will return status: "IN_PROGRESS" or "COMPLETED"
# 4. Due to random failures in inventory (10%) and payment (15%) services,
#    some orders may fail and trigger compensation flow
# 5. Check logs in each service terminal to see the event flow
# 6. Monitor RabbitMQ management UI at http://localhost:15672
